Sval: the tab switcher leaves a Quick Peek's page active

A Quick Peek (SvalQuickPeek) is a hidden background tab whose panel shows over the
selected tab, and SvalQuickPeek keeps its browser active while it shows, as
`showSplitViewPanels` keeps a split's panes. A tab switch still in flight
when the Quick Peek opens takes the Quick Peek's tab into its own record once the
page's layers arrive (`getTabState`), then unloads it as a tab nobody
asked to see (`unloadNonRequiredTabs`): the page stops rendering and reads
as hidden. The switcher spares print preview, split view and
Picture-in-Picture pages through `shouldDeactivateDocShell`; no chrome
API adds another, so it asks Tabbrowser.showsOverTab, which names the
tab SvalQuickPeekTab marks.

